            <ArticleTitle>Hemicrania continua responsive to verapamil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1082-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hemicrania continua (HC) is a rare headache syndrome, typically responsive to indomethacin, although patients resistant to this drug have been described. Few treatment alternatives have been proposed in the literature. We here report a patient with HC whose initial excellent response to indomethacin faded but then responded remarkably to verapamil.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
